-- #1311: `NT`'s constructor `Wrap` is module-private BY DESIGN (a `newtype`'s
-- constructor is unconditionally private; `public` is a parse error on `newtype`).
-- Importing it wildcard (`NT(..)`) and using `Wrap` produces a bare `T-UNBOUND` at
-- the USE site -- no mention of the import, no rule, no remedy. Zero resolve
-- diagnostics are emitted; the import line itself is never flagged.
-- Contrast: the analogous abstract-`data` case (control.mdk's sibling shape, see
-- claim.txt) is refused at RESOLVE, ON THE IMPORT MEMBER, with the rule and the
-- remedy embedded in the message.
import nmod.{NT(..), unNT}

main = println (unNT (Wrap 5))
